A parentheses string is valid if and only if:

It is the empty string,
It can be written as AB (A concatenated with B), where A and B are valid strings, or
It can be written as (A), where A is a valid string.


   int minAddToMakeValid(string s) {
        
        
        int ans = 0,bal = 0;
        
        for(int i=0;i<s.size();i++){
            bal+=s[i]=='('?+1:-1;
            if(bal==-1){
                ans++;
                bal++;
            }
        }
        return ans + bal;
        
    }
    ****************************************************************************************************
    here if the bal is -1 that means we have encountered a ')' so we have only one choice of increasing the ans and set the balance to 0 (meaning to insert '(')
    also if bal is > 0 at the end this means we have encountered few ((( so we have to have some ))) to balance them that's why we add them.
